&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Launch and lifecycle ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive the full product lifecycle from early concept through general availability and post-launch iteration. You will make clear calls on scope, sequence, and tradeoffs while owning the outcome of what ships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Discovery and market intelligence:&lt;/strong&gt; Run continuous discovery with enterprise customers and prospects to understand complex workflows, compliance needs, and buying expectations. You will separate table-stakes requirements from differentiation opportunities and synthesize findings into actionable product decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with engineering to sequence and scope work, and partner with design on interaction models and user experience. You will hold the quality bar for acceptance criteria, dependency management, sprint discipline, and delivery readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Go-to-market partnership:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the subject-matter expert for Sales, Customer Success, Marketing, and Partnerships on your product area. You will translate product capability into a clear commercial narrative and bring customer and market signals back into the roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-accelerated product work:&lt;/strong&gt; Apply AI across the product cycle, including discovery synthesis, early wireframe concepts, specification drafting, competitive analysis, and design exploration. You will use AI to move faster from insight to decision and share effective practices with the broader team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standards and craft:&lt;/strong&gt; Document decisions, write specs that engineering can act on without a verbal walkthrough, and bring a clear point of view to design reviews. You will ensure the quality of the product area reflects the quality of the thinking behind it.&lt;/li&gt;
